<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Abatis Line</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Great Abatis Belt, Zasechnaya cherta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Abatis Line was a defensive line of felled trees, earthworks and forts built by Muscovy in the sixteenth and early seventeenth centuries to protect its southern lands from Crimean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> raids. Running for hundreds of kilometres south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> through towns such as Tula, it was later superseded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgorod-line">Belgorod Line</a> further south.</p></div>
